d socially responsible citizens with respect and understanding of the diversity that exists in our culture and society.\nAn Overview of Lokapriya Gopinath Bordoloi girls college\nL.G.B Girls’ College is one of the premier institution of women’s education located in the cultural capital of Assam, Tezpur. Since its inception in 1979, the college aims for the holistic development of women students enabling them to make a meaning contribution to the society and nation. The institution hopes to play a lead role in capacity building of the students preparing them for a pioneering and creative role in the development of the nation and to ensure active and equal participation in the process of decision making in all spheres of life. ...\nContinue Reading\nWelcome to Lokapriya Gopinath Bordoloi Girls' College\nOnline Portal\nDepartment Login\nStaff Login\nIQAC\nNSS\nDownload\nDigital Library\nLibrary Reader\nPUBLICATIONS\nCollege\r\n                                    Publication\nFaculty\r\n                                    Publication\nPrincipal\nDr. Tapan Kr. Kalita\n(Principal)\nWelcome to Lokapriya Gopinath Bordoloi Girls' College....\nRead More\nAdmission\n2026-05-29\nFYUGP ARREAR II & IV SEMESTER FORM FILL UP NOTICE\nClick Here\n2026-05-14\nCBCS 2ND SEMESTER(ARREAR) PROGRAMME 2026\nClick Here\n2026-02-18\nSUBJECT WITH PAPER CODE\nClick Here\n2026-05-08\nFYUGP 1ST SEMESTER ADMISSION NOTICE\nClick Here\n2024-06-10\nFEE WAIVER SCHEME 2024-25 SESSION\nClick Here\nView All\nNews & Notice Board\n2026-05-29\nFYUGP ARREAR II & IV SEMESTER FORM FILL UP NOTICE\nClick Here\n2026-05-14\nCBCS 2ND SEMESTER(ARREAR) PROGRAMME 2026\nClick Here\n2026-02-18\nSUBJECT WITH PAPER CODE\nClick Here\n2026-05-08\nFYUGP 1ST SEMESTER ADMISSION NOTICE\nClick Here\n2024-06-10\nFEE WAIVER SCHEME 2024-25 SESSION\nClick Here\nView All\nTender Report\nView All\nQuick Links\nU.G.C.\nN.A.A.C.\nSWAYAM\nE-Pathsala\nAchievments\nView All\nProf. Nani Gopal Mahanta inaugurated the book titled ” National Education Policy 2020: Issues and Challenges”.\n2022-11-11\nNational Seminar on “National Education Policy – 2020: Issues & Challenges” held at LGB Girl’s College.\n2023-11-11\nProf. Nani Gopal Mahanta, Education Advisor, Government of Assam, gracing the event as the Chief Guest of National Seminar on “NEP – 2020: Issues & Challenges” held at LGB Girls' College.\n2022-11-11\nDistribution of food items by L.G.B Girls' College authorities.\n2022-05-21\n10-day Yoga training organized at L.G.B Girls' College.\n2022-06-03\nWinter clothes distribution drive for deprived children and adults in remote areas to ensure their safety in the winters organised by L.G.B Girls' College, NSS Unit.\n2023-01-08\nUnit of blood has been donated by the students of L.G.B Girls' college, NSS Unit at TMCH.\n2023-01-02\nWinter clothes distribution drive for deprived children and adults in remote areas to ensure their safety in the winters organised by L.G.B Girls' College, NSS Unit.\n2023-01-04\nNSS Unit of L.G.B Girls' College has participated in Rashtriya Yuva Mahotsav 2023.\n2023-01-29\nWinter clothes distribution drive for deprived children and adults in remote areas to ensure their safety in the winters organised by L.G.B Girls' College, NSS Unit.\n2023-01-04\nL.G.B Girls' College celebrated Lachit Divas (400th Birth anniversary of Bir Lachit Borphukan).\n2022-11-19\nWorld Bicycle Day 2022 observed on 3rd June in L.G.B Girls' College.\n2022-06-03\nYoga session held in L.G.B Girls' College.\n2022-06-03\nL.G.B Girls' College distributed food and other relief materials to flood victims in their adopted village.\n2022-05-21\nBarnali Devi, NSS Programme Officer of L.G.B Girls' College got NSS State Award.\n2022-01-16\n04 volunteers’ (Puja Chetry, Niha Boro, Nishita Medhi, Sonamaina Rabha) selected for pre Re-public day. The PRD Camp was held in Bhubaneswar.\n2020-11-19\n04 volunteers’ (Puja Chetry, Niha Boro, Nishita Medhi, Sonamaina Rabha) selected for pre Re-public day. The PRD Camp was held in Bhubaneswar from 22.11.2020.\n2020-11-19\nStudents from L.G.B Girls' College successfully completed Mountaineering-related activities including traditional outdoor climbing on 19/11/2016.\n2016-11-19\nNational Service Scheme, Assam State Level Award 2019-20 presented to Sri Bornali Devi Programme Officer (NSS), LGB Girls' College.\n2022-01-12\nNational Service Scheme, Assam State Level Award 2019-20 presented to Sri Bornali Devi Programme Officer (NSS), LGB Girls' College.\n2022-01-12\nNSS State Award for LGB Girls' College.\n2022-01-12\nNSS Programme Officer from our College got selected as a contingent leader at NIC Camp held in Rajasthan. We also received National Best Management Award.\n2021-03-20\n04 volunteers’ (Puja Chetry, Niha Boro, Nishita Medhi, Sonamaina Rabha) selected for pre Re-public day. The PRD Camp was held in Bhubaneswar from 22.11.2020.\n2020-11-22\nL.G.B Girls' College received Assam “N.S.S State Award\".\n2022-01-12\nVolunteers from G.U as well as from five different colleges have participated in the North-East NSS festival on 16.01.2020. Our N.S.S Unit two volunteers’ selected Daisy Basumatary and Manju Devi.\n2020-01-16\nOur selected N.S.S Volunteers’ Dikshita Bora and Borsa Mochahary participated in National Adventure Camp held at Nimas.\n2022-03-30\n04 NSS volunteers' from LGB Girls' college got selected to participate in North East NSS Festival in Itanagar, Arunachal Pradesh. (Niha Boro, Yokta Subedi, Priya Boro, Aditi Bora).\n2021-03-07\nNational Librarian's Day observed at L.G.B Girl's College, Tezpur.\n2022-08-17\nBook Fair.\n2018-10-02\nStudents Achievement.\n2018-09-26\nEnvironmental Awareness Programme.\n2022-06-06\nL.G.B Girls' College wins first prize in skit competition organised by LGBRIMH on 10th Sept, 2018.\n2018-09-10\nPrevious\nNext\nDownload\nView All\n2022-12-27\nRules and Regulations for Girls' Hostel and Hostel Identity Card Form.\nClick Here\nEvents\nView All\nWorkshop on Academic and Administrative Audit organized 